 1. Executive Summary
The AI Interview Coach is a full-stack application that uses Large Language Models (LLMs) via Ollama and LangGraph for workflow orchestration to conduct intelligent mock interviews. Users upload resumes, answer interview questions sequentially, and receive AI-powered feedback.
Key Objectives
•	Generate role-specific interview questions based on resume analysis
•	Provide sequential, user-friendly interview experience
•	Deliver personalized feedback and scoring on answers
•	Ensure resilience with graceful degradation when LLM unavailable
•	Maintain clean, maintainable, and scalable architecture
 2. System Overview
Architecture Diagram
The system consists of three main components working together:
• Streamlit Frontend (Port 8501) - User interface
• FastAPI Backend (Port 8000) - REST API server
• Ollama Service (Port 11434) - Local LLM for AI processing
Technology Stack
Layer	Technology	Purpose
Frontend	Streamlit	Interactive web UI
Backend	FastAPI	REST API server
Server	Uvicorn	ASGI server
Orchestration	LangGraph	Workflow DAG
LLM	Ollama	Local language models
File Processing	PyPDF2, python-docx	Resume parsing
Database	SQLite	State checkpointing
HTTP Client	Requests	API communication
 3. Architecture Layers
Layer 1: User Interface (Streamlit)
Responsibilities:
•	Display resume upload form
•	Show interview questions one at a time
•	Capture and store user answers
•	Display evaluation results with scores
•	Enable navigation between questions
•	Provide progress tracking
•	Allow report download
Layer 2: API (FastAPI)
Responsibilities:
•	Handle POST /analyze endpoint (resume upload + question generation)
•	Handle POST /evaluate endpoint (answer scoring)
•	Validate input data
•	Manage CORS for cross-origin requests
•	Implement timeout protection (60 seconds)
•	Provide structured error responses
•	Log all activities
Layer 3: Graph Processing (LangGraph)
Workflow Steps:
Step	Function
1	parse_resume_node - Extract resume insights
2	identify_gaps_node - Find skill gaps
3	generate_questions_node - Create interview questions
4	generate_feedback_node - Generate preparation tips
5	evaluate_answers_node - Score answers
6	finalize_report_node - Generate JSON report
Layer 4: Tools & Utilities
Key Functions:
•	load_resume_text() - Parse PDF, DOCX, TXT files
•	extract_resume_insights() - Call Ollama for resume analysis
•	build_interview_questions() - Generate questions with fallback
•	evaluate_user_answers() - Score and provide feedback
•	save_report() - Write results to JSON
Layer 5: Ollama Client
Features:
•	Service availability check (1-second timeout)
•	Automatic model selection and fallback
•	Request timeout protection (2 seconds)
•	Graceful error handling
•	No indefinite hangs
 4. Components & Modules
frontend.py
Type: Streamlit UI
Description: Resume upload, question display, results visualization
app.py
Type: FastAPI Server
Description: REST API endpoints, request routing, error handling
graph.py
Type: LangGraph DAG
Description: Workflow definition, state management
nodes.py
Type: Processing Nodes
Description: Individual processing steps in workflow
tools.py
Type: Utility Functions
Description: Resume parsing, text processing, report generation
ollama_client.py
Type: LLM Integration
Description: Ollama communication with timeout protection
prompts.py
Type: Prompt Templates
Description: AI instruction prompts for various tasks
state.py
Type: State Schema
Description: TypedDict definitions for InterviewState
database.py
Type: Data Persistence
Description: SQLite initialization and management
 5. Data Flow
Interview Generation Flow
1. User uploads resume file and enters role/experience
2. Frontend sends POST /analyze request
3. Backend parses resume (PyPDF2/python-docx)
4. LangGraph executes workflow with 60-second timeout
5. Each node processes data and calls Ollama when needed
6. Fallback mechanisms activate if Ollama unavailable
7. Results returned with generated questions
8. Frontend displays questions sequentially
Answer Evaluation Flow
1. User enters answers for all questions
2. Frontend sends POST /evaluate request
3. Backend calls evaluate_user_answers() for each answer
4. Ollama evaluates answer and assigns score (0-10)
5. If Ollama unavailable, fallback scoring used
6. Evaluations returned with scores and feedback
7. Frontend displays results and allows report download
 6. Technology Stack
Language: Python 3.8+
Frontend Framework: Streamlit
Backend Framework: FastAPI
Web Server: Uvicorn
Workflow Orchestration: LangGraph
LLM Service: Ollama (local)
Resume Parsing: PyPDF2, python-docx
Database: SQLite3
HTTP Client: Requests
Logging: Python logging module
 7. API Endpoints
POST /analyze
Purpose: Upload resume and generate interview questions
Request Parameters:
•	• role (string) - Target job role
• experience (string) - Years of experience
• resume_file (file) - PDF, DOCX, or TXT file
Response:
• success (boolean) - Request status
• result (object) - Contains questions, summary, gaps
• report_path (string) - Path to generated report
POST /evaluate
Purpose: Score and provide feedback on answers
Request Parameters:
• role (string) - Job role
• questions (array) - Interview questions
• answers (object) - User answers by question
Response:
• success (boolean) - Request status
• evaluations (array) - Scores and feedback for each answer
 8. Error Handling
Timeout Protection
• Request timeout: 120 seconds (frontend to backend)
• Graph execution timeout: 60 seconds
• Ollama request timeout: 2 seconds
• Ollama socket check: 1 second
• Fallback triggers if any timeout occurs
Graceful Degradation
When Ollama is unavailable:
• Default interview questions are provided
• Heuristic resume summaries are generated
• Simple length-based scoring is used
• Generic preparation tips are shown
• System remains fully functional
Error Response Format
All errors return JSON with structure:
{"success": false, "error": "error message"}
 9. Deployment Architecture
Development (Current)
Single Windows/Linux machine running:
• Streamlit (port 8501)
• FastAPI (port 8000)
• Ollama (port 11434)
• SQLite (local file storage)
Production Recommendation
Distributed architecture with:
• Load balancer for incoming requests
• Multiple FastAPI instances
• Dedicated Ollama service
• PostgreSQL database
• Redis cache layer
• Cloud storage for reports
 10. Key Design Decisions
Timeout Protection
Rationale: Prevents indefinite hangs when Ollama unavailable
Sequential Questions
Rationale: Improves UX compared to large form
Stateless API
Rationale: Enables horizontal scaling
LangGraph Workflow
Rationale: Provides clarity and testability
Graceful Fallbacks
Rationale: Ensures functionality even without LLM
Local Ollama
Rationale: Maintains data privacy, no API costs
